*======================================================================
* txaeng.a99 - the engine build: the VM at >A000, the kernel at >2000.
*
* tools/build.py assembles this twice: once to learn the engine's size,
* then again with gen/storysrc.a99 saying which cartridge bank the story
* starts in.  The resident engine must end below >D000: window D (text)
* is mapped over >D000 while the story runs.  build.py checks.
*======================================================================
       COPY "macros.a99"
       COPY "defs.a99"

       AORG >A000
       COPY "engine.a99"
       COPY "vm.a99"
       COPY "vmmem.a99"
       COPY "output.a99"
       COPY "input.a99"
       COPY "undo.a99"
       COPY "save.a99"
       COPY "fast.a99"
       COPY "stload.a99"
       COPY "gen/storysrc.a99"
* ENGND: first free byte of the resident window
ENGND

       AORG >2000
KENTRY B    @START             the entry: E/A 5 and the cartridge start here
       COPY "vdp.a99"
       COPY "f18a.a99"
       COPY "pager.a99"
       COPY "keys.a99"
       COPY "text80.a99"
       COPY "disk.a99"
       COPY "picture.a99"
       COPY "sound.a99"
* KERNND: first free byte of the kernel window
KERNND

* The startup code and the font are used only before the story runs, so
* they load where the value stack and the frames will be: once the story
* runs, the stack overwrites them.  (They used to fill the kernel and
* resident windows.)  build.py checks this segment ends below >3800.
       AORG VSTK
       COPY "startup.a99"
       COPY "gen/font.a99"
* STUPND: first byte past the startup segment
STUPND
       END  START
